      "writtenOn": "2019-03-06T09:41:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this synchronized block necessary? It wasn\u0027t there before, and IIRC this code is always ever run on the same thread (i.e., the Handler thread). It seems like it would be simpler to do one of the following:\n\n1. Move the callback registration and unregistration to the handler thread. In other words, have registerTetheringEventCallback and unregisterTetheringEventCallback just post a lambda to the Handler. I think this can be done because these functions do not return anything. Also ISTM that even if the caller calls register() and unregister() one after the other (or even on different threads?), it\u0027s still safe because the operations will be done in the correct order.\n\n2. Instead of locking on mPublicSync, lock on mTetheringEventCallbacks. If possible (but it may not be possible to do it correctly) it would be even better to just move the locking inside reportUpstreamChangedLocked(), registerTetheringEventCallback and unregisterTetheringEventCallback.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1240,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 1240,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "815307c5ba9c51a6e2ea920caa2ad2828f402b0d",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
